# Force LF regardless of the cloning platform's git config. Most of this
# repo (shell scripts, Dockerfiles, nginx configs) runs inside Linux
# containers, and a shebang broken by a stray \r fails opaquely on Windows
# clones ("bash\r: No such file or directory" instead of a clear error).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch files are the exception to the LF rule above. Not because LF was
# observed to break one - it was tested on Windows 11 and parsed fine - but
# because cmd.exe has a long history of mis-parsing LF-only scripts around
# labels and goto, setup.cmd uses both, and this costs nothing.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
